<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-PRIX JACQUES LE MAROIS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-PRIX JACQUES LE MAROIS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DEAUVILLE, France 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Prix</p>
<p>Jacques Le Marois, a group one race for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over one mile (1.6 km) on Sunday:</p>
<p> 1. Spinning World	   (ridden by Cash Asmussen)</p>
<p> 2. Daylami		    (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p> 3. Neuilly		    (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>Six ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Two lengths, six lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Niarchos Family and trained in France by</p>
<p>Jonathan Pease.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (including a one-franc stake): Win 3.9. Places</p>
<p>2.0, 2.0. Straight forecast 15.3.</p>
</text>
